    "title": "Brazil get back on track with victory over Croatia (3-1)",
    "text": "International friendlyComments© Rich Storry/Getty ImagesDanilo scored for Brazil in the first halfIn the international friendly in Orlando, Brazil got back on track after losing to France a few days ago. It was an important 3-1 victory against Croatia that left good feelings.The better team won on Tuesday night as Brazil were sharper than Croatia. In the first half, they had a few clear chances that Dominik Livakovic stopped. However, a great counterattack from Vinicius left Danilo open in the box for the opening goal.Not much happened in the second half until a long pass allowed Croatia to tie through Lovro Mayer, with the help of Bento’s poor intervention. Luckily for Brazil, they responded quickly with a penalty scored by Igor Thiago, after a foul won by Endrick, who also assisted Martinelli for the final goal to give the fans some relief.Brazil win the match 3-1.92' Endrick played a through ball on the counterattack for Martinelli, who finished to score.88' Endrick goes down in the box after a touch from Šutalo, Thiago scored the penalty kick.83' Mayer scores for Croatia following a poor clearance by Bento.74' Moro took a shot from the edge of the box, but it went just wide. 09:34PMNo clear dominator70' After numerous substitutions, neither team is controlling the match. 09:30PMVinícius substitution66' Vinícius is taken off after providing an assist, with Martinelli coming on. 09:23PMModrić substitution59' Modrić is taken off as part of a four-player change.56' Brazil are letting Croatia have possession to look for a counterattack. 09:09PMSecond half beginsThe teams are back on the field to start the second half.Brazil are the better side and lead 1-0.45 + 1' A great counterattack from Brazil, Vinícius cut inside and set it up for Danilo, who finished for the goal.45' Modrić delivered a free kick, Vušković met it with a header, but it was a great save by Bento.41' Cunha struck from outside the box aiming for the corner, but Livaković got down well to make the save.40' Perišić delivered a cross from the left, Kramarić hit a volley, but a deflection made it easy for Bento.36' Modrić lost the ball again, Cunha played it through to João Pedro, but his finish was well saved by Livaković.23' A set-piece routine saw Danilo play it to Cunha, whose right-footed shot deflected off a defender and went just wide of the goal.20' Modrić gave the ball away with a poor back pass that was picked off by Vinícius, who laid it off centrally for Danilo, but his shot was well saved by Livaković. 08:20PMBrazil on the ball16' Brazil have regained possession, but it has not been very effective.11' Croatia look a bit more dangerous on the wings, but they are not creating clear chances.6' Both teams trade possession in the opening minutes.The match is underway between Brazil and Croatia. 07:45PMConfirmed lineup for CroatiaDominik Livaković; Josip Stanišić, Duje Caleta-car, Luka Vušković; Josip Sutalo, Martin Baturina, Petar Susić, Luka Modrić, Ivan Perišić; Andrej Kramarić, Ante Budimir. 07:30PMConfirmed lineup for BrazilBento; Ibañez, Marquinhos, Leo Pereira, Douglas Santos; Casemiro, Danilo; Matheus Cunha, Luiz Henrique, Vinicius; João Pedro. 07:15PMBrazil and Croatia World Cup groupsThe group stage picture is now set for both sides as they look ahead to the World Cup. Brazil are in Group C with Morocco, Haiti and Scotland, while Croatia are in Group L alongside England, Panama and Ghana.The match venue is Camping World Stadium in Orlando, Florida. It has a capacity of 60,000.You can watch Brazil vs Croatia on Fubo, DirecTV Stream, and ESPN Deportes in the USA.Welcome to live coverage of the international friendly Brazil vs Croatia.200+ Channels & Local SportsPrice: Plans starting at $14.99/mo (Latino)Watch Ligue 1, Copa Libertadores & World Cup QualifiersEvery MLS Match in One PlacePrice: $12.99/mo (Now included with standard subscription)Watch every MLS regular season game, Playoffs & Leagues CupMany Sports & ESPN OriginalsPrice: $1